## Part 1 — content removed as derivable (≈2,020 est. tokens)

### A. Directory Structure tree — 26 lines, 1,580 chars, ~395 est. tokens

`ls`/`find` shows the tree. Every non-obvious annotation in it was already
restated elsewhere **in the same file**: `input-notes/` → the "Notes vs Resumes
(CRITICAL)" section; `processed/` → Key Rules; `input-voice-samples/` → the
`create-cover-letter` skill.

### B. Agent System roster (7 numbered entries) — 10 lines, 680 chars, ~170 est. tokens

Verbatim from the `description:` frontmatter of `.claude/agents/*.md`, which is
**already resident** in the agent listing every session — so it was being paid
for twice. Replaced with a two-line pointer. The design rationale that follows
it (why a cover letter gets exactly two reviewers) is not derivable and was
kept.

### C. Workflow section — 74 lines, 3,836 chars, ~959 est. tokens

The largest single cut. Every subsection was a prose restatement of a
`SKILL.md` that already loads when its command runs — verified against
`create-resume`, `create-cover-letter`, `parse-resumes`, and `scan-codebase`,
each of which covers its own workflow in more detail than CLAUDE.md did.

Replaced with a command index plus the **two constraints the skills depend on
but cannot enforce**, which were the only non-derivable content in the section:

- `/parse-resumes` must run first; `profile.json` is the single source of truth.
- Documents are generated only by `tools/generate_resume.py` and
  `tools/generate_cover_letter.py` — never inline python-docx.

### D. Tools table (13 scripts) — 14 lines, 2,033 chars, ~508 est. tokens

`ls tools/` plus `--help` (every script uses argparse, 5–8 arguments each).
Replaced with one line saying exactly that. **Kept**: the directive above the
table ("skills must call these scripts — never generate new scripts or write
inline code"), and the `common.py` / `layout.py` notes below it, which explain
*why* those modules exist rather than what they contain.

### E. Dry Runs section — 5 lines, 212 chars, ~53 est. tokens

`--dry-run` is declared in both generators' argparse. Its one useful sentence
(use it to check a page target before writing a file) was folded into the Tools
section instead of dropped.

