## Part 2 — content moved to lazy loading (≈450 est. tokens)

This content is worth keeping but only matters in one context, so it now loads
in that context instead of always.

### Templates section → `.claude/rules/resume-formatting.md`

25 lines, 1,249 chars, ~312 est. tokens.

That rule file already declares `paths: templates/**`, so it attaches exactly
when someone touches a template — which is the only time these gotchas apply
(body content is stripped; the template must define `Normal` and `List Bullet`;
a missing `--template` path is an error, not a silent fallback). Moved
verbatim.

### DOCX Extraction Failsafe → `.claude/skills/parse-resumes/SKILL.md`

10 lines, 556 chars, ~139 est. tokens.

The extractor only runs during `/parse-resumes`, and that skill already invokes
`extract_resumes.py`. The failsafe text now sits directly after the step that
parses the extractor's JSON output — closer to the point of use than it was in
CLAUDE.md. Moved verbatim, under a new `#### Extraction failsafe` heading.

